<script module>
  import Demo from "$ui/components/Demo.abide"
  import Panel from "$ui/components/Panel.abide"
  import DetailsRouteDemo from "$ui/demos/pages/routing/DetailsRouteDemo.abide"
  import { navigate } from "abide/ui/navigate"
</script>


<main class="page">
  <h1 data-testid="details-heading">Details</h1>
  <p class="lead">A static sibling route — <code>pages/routing/details/page.abide</code> at <code>/pages/routing/details</code>. Exact routes win over <code>[slug]</code>, so navigating here (link or <code>navigate()</code>) reaches this dedicated page, not the param page.</p>
  <Demo id="details-route" title="Current route" client="src/ui/demos/pages/routing/DetailsRouteDemo.abide" tab="client">
    <DetailsRouteDemo />
  </Demo>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>The same readout from the static sibling. Compare <code>route().name</code> with the param page's: an exact route wins, so this file answered rather than <code>[slug]</code>.</p>
  </aside>
  <Panel id="details-back" title="Back to the hub">
    <div class="row">
      <button data-testid="back-hub" onclick={() => navigate("/pages/routing")}>← back to hub</button>
    </div>
  </Panel>
  <aside class="aside">
    <p>The hub links back here, and this returns — the two halves of the precedence claim, walkable in both directions.</p>
  </aside>
</main>
